# Talkwer quality

## Required checks

- `pnpm verify`
- `pnpm lint`
- `pnpm typecheck`
- `pnpm build`
- `pnpm check:filenames`
- `pnpm check:image-sizes`

## Review checklist

- No visual regressions on active homepage sections.
- No duplicate domain types across feature files.
- No placeholder links (`href="#"`) in active UX paths.
- Accessibility checklist reviewed (`docs/ACCESSIBILITY_CHECKLIST.md`).
- Release checklist reviewed (`docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md`).

## Motion lifecycle

### Choose the motion implementation

- Preserve the authored duration, easing, trigger positions, scrub math, and reduced-motion behavior when changing implementation.
- The default hero uses CSS for its image/overlay entrance and independently masked headline rows. `HeroFrame` provides lightweight scroll updates with the established scroll math; keep the row masks intact.
- The marquee uses a 30-second linear CSS loop to `translateX(-50%)`; reduced motion disables the loop.
- Use `useDeferredGsapContext` from `@/lib/use-deferred-gsap` for below-fold, non-pinned GSAP sections. It waits until the section is within 64px of the viewport, then dynamically imports `@/lib/useGsap` and delegates to `createGsapContext`. Keep the supplied engine inside the callback rather than adding an eager GSAP import.
- Use `useGsapContext` from `@/lib/useGsap` for pinned ScrollTrigger sections. Both context paths retain capture-phase navigation cleanup and context revert; keep target refs scoped to the section root.
- Use plain effects for DOM listeners and other non-GSAP side effects, cleaning up listeners and animation frames on unmount.

### Accessibility

- Respect reduced-motion with `prefersReducedMotion()`.
- Skip non-essential animation when reduced-motion is enabled.

### Performance

- Avoid duplicate ScrollTrigger registrations in component trees.
- Keep timeline creation scoped to the section refs.
- Preserve server-rendered carousel slide markup while the lazy engine loads. Carousel enhancement begins within 400px of the viewport; testimonials import Autoplay asynchronously and skip autoplay for reduced motion.
- ScrollTrigger `pin` is allowed only through `useGsapContext` (it reverts on capture-phase internal navigation / `popstate` before React unmounts). Do not pin outside that hook — pin reparents into `.pin-spacer` and otherwise throws `removeChild` NotFoundError on App Router client navigations. Do not fake pin with inflated section height + `position: sticky` when the sticky panel is taller than the viewport (creates giant blank space).

### Invariants

- No visual drift during refactors.
- No timing/easing/trigger drift during refactors.
- No leaked triggers or stale contexts after navigation/unmount.
